<XPD:BODY><XPD:OBJ name="DocumentElement" type="UMLProject" guid="o6jy5Rz+Q0eRSgL8s9GiMwAA"><XPD:ATTR name="Title" type="string">Passport Application System - Use Case Model</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="#OwnedElements" type="integer">1</XPD:ATTR><XPD:OBJ name="OwnedElements[0]" type="UMLModel" guid="krGTNZTTSbKWx5n0gmNumwAA"><XPD:ATTR name="Name" type="string">Use Case Model</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="StereotypeProfile" type="string">UMLStandard</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="StereotypeName" type="string">useCaseModel</XPD:ATTR><XPD:REF name="Namespace">o6jy5Rz+Q0eRSgL8s9GiMwAA</XPD:REF><XPD:ATTR name="Documentation" type="string">Source: pas.md class definitions, operations, relationships and ambiguity notes. Use case interpretation of the supplied system design. Applicant, Officer and Police Verification Staff are human actors; Payment Gateway and Police Verification System are external actors. User is the account superclass, not an additional actor goal. No dependency of appointments on a particular application is assumed. Police staff and the external police system support the verification use case without assuming a mandatory joint workflow. Police findings are not restricted to officer decision outcomes. Rejection/return remarks are mandatory for those outcomes. Receipt is generated only after a successful payment. Notification channels are email/SMS, with no invented gateway actor. Status update and notification timing are operational interpretations, with conditions recorded on relationships. Officer functions require authorization.</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="#OwnedDiagrams" type="integer">1</XPD:ATTR><XPD:OBJ name="OwnedDiagrams[0]" type="UMLUseCaseDiagram" guid="DknPsZluSYSb069LDt02OgAA"><XPD:ATTR name="Name" type="string">Passport Application System - Use Cases</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="DefaultDiagram" type="boolean">True</XPD:ATTR><XPD:REF name="DiagramOwner">krGTNZTTSbKWx5n0gmNumwAA</XPD:REF><XPD:OBJ name="DiagramView" type="UMLUseCaseDiagramView" guid="Rv5YDWDpQJGCRPRMoPzIMQAA"><XPD:REF name="Diagram">DknPsZluSYSb069LDt02OgAA</XPD:REF><XPD:ATTR name="#OwnedViews" type="integer">45</XPD:ATTR><XPD:OBJ name="OwnedViews[0]" type="UMLSystemBoundaryView" guid="gBMt/c4lQwqdgr0/CXoY6QAA">
